WEBVTT

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:18.952
MAN:
Captain's log,
stardate 57436.2.

00:00:18.996 --> 00:00:21.738
TheCerritos is docked
at Douglas Station

00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:24.828
for routine maintenance
and resupply.

00:00:24.871 --> 00:00:26.873
We will soon set course
for the capital planet

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.832
on the Galar system,
where we're scheduled

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:32.401
to make second contact with
the Galardonian high council.

00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:34.098
First contact is a delicate,

00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:36.274
high-stakes
operation of diplomacy.

00:00:36.318 --> 00:00:39.451
One must be ready for anything
when humanity is interacting

00:00:39.495 --> 00:00:42.541
with an alien race
for the first time.

00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:44.674
But we don't do that.

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:46.676
Our specialty is second contact.

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:47.677
Still pretty important.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.157
We get all the paperwork signed,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.984
make sure we're spelling
the name of the planet right,

00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:52.595
get to know
all the good places to eat.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.033
Oh, my God.
What are you doing?

00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:57.643
-Uh, nothing, nothing, nothing.
I'm just...
-Oh, no.

00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:59.428
-Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:00:59.471 --> 00:01:01.125
-Are you pretending to do
a captain's log?

00:01:01.169 --> 00:01:02.953
- We're all supposed
to keep logs.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.868
-Okay, let me listen to it.
-No. Go away.

00:01:04.911 --> 00:01:06.174
-Leave me alone. No. No.
-Ah! I can't believe

00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.740
you're wasting
your shore leave on this.

00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:09.264
-Privacy, please.
-Aah! Hey, time to go.

00:01:09.307 --> 00:01:10.221
-Come on. Get out of
your little closet.
-Privacy.

00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:11.875
-Let's go. Come on.

00:01:11.918 --> 00:01:12.876
Are you drunk?

00:01:12.919 --> 00:01:14.138
Yeah, dude, you should be, too.

00:01:14.182 --> 00:01:15.661
I mean, this station is amazing.

00:01:15.705 --> 00:01:17.141
And they have Romulan whiskey.

00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:18.795
And I bet you thought
it was going to be green,

00:01:18.838 --> 00:01:20.536
but it is actually blue.
It's this very beautiful color.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.059
Romulan whiskey is
against regulation.

00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:23.626
Yeah, 'cause it's awesome.

00:01:23.669 --> 00:01:25.106
Aw, man, they got
all sorts of great stuff.

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:26.759
Oh! Oh! Come on, check this out.

00:01:26.803 --> 00:01:28.152
- Oh, yeah.
-Ah! Be careful with that!

00:01:28.196 --> 00:01:29.762
Pretty sweet, right?

00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:31.242
Yeah, it's a Klingon bat,
um, bat, uh, bat--

00:01:31.286 --> 00:01:33.244
I don't know. I'm not
a scientist. It doesn't matter.

00:01:33.288 --> 00:01:35.116
-Shut up. I got it from
an old guy with an eye patch.
-Hey, hey.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:37.553
Come spar with me. Come on!
Oh, we can be Klingons.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:39.250
We can have crimped hair,
wrinkled foreheads.

00:01:39.294 --> 00:01:40.991
-Worf, Worf, Worf.
-It's got crusty blood on it!

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.776
-: I love honor!
I demand honor!
-Hey, stop. Stop!

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.255
Wow.

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:13.083
Wow.

00:03:16.304 --> 00:03:17.783
Here we go.

00:03:17.827 --> 00:03:20.003
Ensign D'Vana Tendi,
reporting for duty.

00:03:20.046 --> 00:03:21.613
I'm a transfer from Outpost 79.

00:03:21.657 --> 00:03:23.224
Deck Four.
Follow the yellow line.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:24.573
Take the turbolift
all the way down.

00:03:24.616 --> 00:03:26.052
Thank you so much.

00:03:26.096 --> 00:03:27.576
And can I just say
that I'm really honored to be...

00:03:27.619 --> 00:03:28.881
Keep it moving, lower decks.

00:03:28.925 --> 00:03:30.143
Next!

00:03:31.797 --> 00:03:33.277
REPLICATOR:
Banana, hot.

00:03:33.321 --> 00:03:34.278
Banana, hot.

00:03:34.322 --> 00:03:36.062
Aah! Frickin' burned me.

00:03:36.106 --> 00:03:38.239
Uh, i-is there
an Ensign Boimler here?

00:03:38.282 --> 00:03:39.240
REPLICATOR:
Banana, hot.

00:03:40.328 --> 00:03:41.764
Hi. Here, that's me. Ahoy.

00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:42.808
Ensign Tendi reporting for duty.

00:03:42.852 --> 00:03:44.288
You're my orientation liaison.

00:03:44.332 --> 00:03:46.856
Yes, welcome. Brad Boimler,
Ensign, command division.

00:03:46.899 --> 00:03:48.249
Ah! Oh, my gosh.

00:03:48.292 --> 00:03:49.859
I've never worked
with commanders before.

00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:51.164
I'm in sciences.

00:03:51.208 --> 00:03:53.079
I love science.
Uh, it's so sciency.

00:03:53.123 --> 00:03:54.907
I mean, that blue goes green
with your great--

00:03:54.951 --> 00:03:56.300
-I mean, great, with your--
oh, my gosh.
-Yo-yo, what up?

00:03:56.344 --> 00:03:58.346
Beckett Mariner, also an ensign,
command division,

00:03:58.389 --> 00:04:00.609
but not quite as
impressed with myself

00:04:00.652 --> 00:04:02.611
as this little rascal over here.

00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:04.221
Yeah, we're not actual
commanders, by the way,

00:04:04.265 --> 00:04:06.092
-we're more like
commanders-in-training.

00:04:06.136 --> 00:04:08.007
I can't believe
we're gonna serve side by side,

00:04:08.051 --> 00:04:10.314
scientists and commanders,
an elite team.

00:04:10.358 --> 00:04:11.881
Yeah, no,
we're not really elite.

00:04:11.924 --> 00:04:14.275
We're more like the cool,
scrappy underdogs of the ship.

00:04:14.318 --> 00:04:15.928
You know,
we don't wash our hands,

00:04:15.972 --> 00:04:17.321
we're doing kickflips
all the time.

00:04:17.365 --> 00:04:19.192
But with focus and dedication,

00:04:19.236 --> 00:04:22.326
you could be
chief medical officer someday.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.849
Oh, senior officers
are overrated.

00:04:23.893 --> 00:04:25.024
They're always, like,
stressed out

00:04:25.068 --> 00:04:26.635
and just yelling
about directives.

00:04:26.678 --> 00:04:28.680
It is better down here,
where the real action is.

00:04:28.724 --> 00:04:30.334
You really don't care
about moving up in rank?

00:04:30.378 --> 00:04:32.293
Been there, definitely over it.

00:04:32.336 --> 00:04:34.773
Whenever you think for yourself,
they knock you back down.

00:04:34.817 --> 00:04:36.340
You know, for someone
who claims to hate rank,

00:04:36.384 --> 00:04:38.081
you certainly bring it up a lot.

00:04:38.124 --> 00:04:39.822
Yes, I'm very complicated,
thank you.

00:04:39.865 --> 00:04:42.781
-Ooh, you want the tour?
-O-Of the-the ship? Uh, yes!

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:44.043
You don't like giving the tour.

00:04:44.087 --> 00:04:45.958
True, but I do...

00:04:46.002 --> 00:04:47.308
...have a big box
of shore leave contraband

00:04:47.351 --> 00:04:48.961
I need help with.

00:04:49.005 --> 00:04:51.442
BOIMLER: The senior officers
are all up here,

00:04:51.486 --> 00:04:53.792
then you've got Engineering,
science stations.

00:04:53.836 --> 00:04:57.013
All sorts of ops around here...

00:04:57.056 --> 00:04:59.711
Ops, ops, ops, storage, ops.

00:04:59.755 --> 00:05:01.713
Actually, there's like
a ton of ops.

00:05:01.757 --> 00:05:04.325
-It's like, guys,
I think we have ops covered.

00:05:04.368 --> 00:05:06.327
-And we're here?
-Well, no. We're actually way
down here.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.893
MARINER:
What this map doesn't show you

00:05:07.937 --> 00:05:10.287
is that everything from,
like, this deck up,

00:05:10.331 --> 00:05:11.723
super lame, not important to us.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:12.985
-You like the bar.
-All right, fine.

00:05:13.029 --> 00:05:14.900
-Everything except the bar.
-And the bridge.

00:05:14.944 --> 00:05:15.988
-The bridge is not cool.
-Yes, it is.

00:05:16.032 --> 00:05:17.338
Oh, hey, that's Rutherford.

00:05:17.381 --> 00:05:18.687
Rutherford, what's up?

00:05:21.124 --> 00:05:22.865
Yo, yo, yo, slow down.
Is your thingy acting up?

00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:24.388
Rutherford's an engineer, oh,
and, as of a couple weeks ago,

00:05:24.432 --> 00:05:25.998
cybernetically enhanced.

00:05:26.042 --> 00:05:28.392
Ooh, I've never met
a recent cyborg.

00:05:28.436 --> 00:05:30.742
Hey, nice to meet you.
Welcome to the crew.

00:05:30.786 --> 00:05:32.831
Wait, don't you have a date
with Ensign Barnes tonight?

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.225
-Sure do.
-She's crazy hot.
Are you nervous?

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:38.402
Trying to be, but this thing
keeps tamping it down.

00:05:38.446 --> 00:05:40.186
Yikes. Okay, you got it.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.363
Uh-oh, I'm nervous.
What if I say something stupid?

00:05:42.406 --> 00:05:44.190
What if she doesn't like
the way that I look?

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.845
Ah, I can only look one way.
I can't change it by tonight!

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:48.456
-Better?
-Yeah, thanks.

00:05:48.499 --> 00:05:50.327
What if she hates my jokes?
I don't know any jokes.

00:05:50.371 --> 00:05:51.807
Oh, I'm gonna puke.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.069
What else?

00:05:53.112 --> 00:05:54.331
That's a room
of switches and dials

00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:55.637
you'll never need to go into.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.116
It's actually a pretty important
processing hub.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.510
Nobody knows what that room is.

00:05:59.554 --> 00:06:01.207
It's a pattern-buffer
maintenance access.

00:06:01.251 --> 00:06:02.383
She knows that.
She's being funny.

00:06:02.426 --> 00:06:04.472
Ah, and this is
Boimler's hidey closet,

00:06:04.515 --> 00:06:06.517
where he pretends to be
a captain like a big boy.

00:06:06.561 --> 00:06:07.910
This is not a good tour!

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.043
So, yeah, we kind of sleep
in a hallway.

00:06:11.087 --> 00:06:12.871
It's a little disappointing,

00:06:12.915 --> 00:06:15.091
but eventually, when you rank
up, you get your own room.

00:06:15.134 --> 00:06:17.136
We're pretty close
to the showers, which is nice.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.138
Does get kind of musty, though.

00:06:19.182 --> 00:06:21.532
Which is weird
'cause the showers are sonic.

00:06:21.576 --> 00:06:24.317
Whoa. Whoa.

00:06:25.493 --> 00:06:27.451
It's... perfect.

00:06:27.495 --> 00:06:29.453
Well, once you get settled,
you should probably check in

00:06:29.497 --> 00:06:31.107
with Nurse Westlake in Medical.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.369
You'll be assisting him
with some basic...

00:06:32.413 --> 00:06:34.066
Ooh, let's go check out
the holodeck.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.894
-She doesn't have time for that.
-How do you know?

00:06:35.938 --> 00:06:37.069
Because I'm her liaison.

00:06:37.113 --> 00:06:38.462
Oh, yeah, then what time is it?

00:06:38.506 --> 00:06:40.986
And don't check, because
if she doesn't have time,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.858
then you should know
what time it is.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.121
Otherwise, you're just trying
to sound important.

00:06:45.164 --> 00:06:47.428
So, what time is it?

00:06:47.471 --> 00:06:48.820
Welcome to the holodeck.

00:06:48.864 --> 00:06:50.256
Easily the best part
of the ship.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.128
The warp core is
the best part of the ship,

00:06:52.171 --> 00:06:53.346
uh, followed by the bridge,

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.044
the photon torpedo tubes,
cetacean ops...

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:56.785
Dude, the warp core is just
a big glowing tube.

00:06:56.828 --> 00:06:59.004
I love the warp core.
The warp core rules.

00:06:59.048 --> 00:07:00.266
No, it doesn't.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.268
Computer,
find us a beach in Hawaii.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.488
What is this?

00:07:04.532 --> 00:07:07.404
This stuff is crazy.
What does it do?

00:07:07.448 --> 00:07:09.101
Oh, it just gets everywhere
and gives you a rash.

00:07:09.145 --> 00:07:10.407
You get a rash from sand?

00:07:10.451 --> 00:07:11.974
-What, you don't?
-No. Nobody does.

00:07:12.017 --> 00:07:13.889
Oh, God, I always do.

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:15.499
Go ahead, take her for a spin.

00:07:15.543 --> 00:07:18.546
Computer, can you put us in
the Adashake Center on Orion?

00:07:20.156 --> 00:07:23.115
Wow, I never made time
to go before I enlisted.

00:07:23.159 --> 00:07:26.249
Pretty cool, right? You can go
almost anywhere you can imagine.

00:07:26.292 --> 00:07:28.164
-Come on, Boimler.
Give it a whirl.
-I-I don't know.

00:07:28.207 --> 00:07:30.514
Come on, there has to be
somewhere you'd love to be.

00:07:30.558 --> 00:07:33.474
Um...
Computer, show us the warp core.

00:07:34.562 --> 00:07:36.477
Wow! Amazing.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.870
What an impressive feat
of engineering.

00:07:38.914 --> 00:07:41.003
You really bum me out sometimes.

00:07:41.046 --> 00:07:42.439
STEVENS :
Ensign Boimler,
report to the bridge.

00:07:42.483 --> 00:07:44.267
You work on the bridge?

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.747
Yeah. That's right.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.053
Because they appreciate people
who follow the rules.

00:07:48.097 --> 00:07:49.402
Who's boring now?

00:07:49.446 --> 00:07:50.621
On my way.

00:07:50.665 --> 00:07:52.536
Wow, does he get
to go up there a lot?

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.886
Nah, just whenever someone
spills a drink or something.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.540
Computer, load Mariner program

00:07:56.584 --> 00:07:58.368
"all-nude Olympic
training facility."

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.152
You might want to back up a bit.

00:08:02.198 --> 00:08:05.157
Wow, this is
a very detailed program.

00:08:14.384 --> 00:08:15.864
Farewell, Commander.

00:08:15.907 --> 00:08:17.518
Thanks again for
your hospitality, Chancellor.

00:08:17.561 --> 00:08:20.346
We'll be sending construction
teams down to help with the...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.174
to help with
the subspace comm array

00:08:22.218 --> 00:08:24.002
as soon as we load up
the supplies.

00:08:24.046 --> 00:08:26.527
Ransom to Cerritos.
Five to beam up.

00:08:31.662 --> 00:08:33.359
Should you get that looked at,
sir?

00:08:33.403 --> 00:08:35.057
Eh, I'll be fine.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.363
-Want to grab a drink tonight?
- You know it.

00:08:37.407 --> 00:08:40.541
Nothing like a cold beer
after a smooth second contact.

00:08:40.584 --> 00:08:42.107
Now,
that's what I'm talking about.

00:08:42.151 --> 00:08:44.545
Oh, yeah.

00:08:46.677 --> 00:08:49.375
TURBOLIFT:
Bridge.

00:08:56.078 --> 00:08:57.949
Ensign.

00:08:57.993 --> 00:09:00.212
Sorry, what?

00:09:00.256 --> 00:09:03.085
I said why aren't you
at your post, Ensign?

00:09:03.128 --> 00:09:04.956
Ransom, report.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.958
Coordination with the
Galardonian high council

00:09:07.002 --> 00:09:08.438
is ahead of schedule, Captain.

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:09.613
Excellent. Keep me posted.

00:09:09.657 --> 00:09:11.659
Ensign, you're with me.

00:09:15.184 --> 00:09:16.489
Brad Boimler.

00:09:16.533 --> 00:09:19.971
Born Modesto, California,
commissioned in '79.

00:09:20.015 --> 00:09:22.452
Not a single demerit.
You keep a personal log?

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.715
-Sometimes five a day.
-That's excessive.

00:09:24.759 --> 00:09:26.630
Do you see a captain's chair
in your future?

00:09:26.674 --> 00:09:29.111
-I hope so, ma'am.
-Well, I see a lot of potential

00:09:29.154 --> 00:09:32.636
in you, son, which is why I'm
giving you a special assignment.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.247
Really? I mean, of course,
yes, whatever you need.

00:09:35.291 --> 00:09:36.988
Keep an eye on Ensign Mariner.

00:09:37.032 --> 00:09:40.165
If she breaks protocol,
I want a full report.

00:09:40.209 --> 00:09:42.690
Sorry, ma'am,
is something wrong?

00:09:42.733 --> 00:09:45.431
I like my crew working
in lockstep.

00:09:45.475 --> 00:09:47.608
There isn't any wiggle room
on the Cerritos.

00:09:47.651 --> 00:09:50.611
Not when lives are at stake.
Do you disagree?

00:09:50.654 --> 00:09:53.048
-No, ma'am.
-Good. Dismissed.

00:09:53.091 --> 00:09:56.965
Ensign, let's keep this
between us, shall we?

00:09:59.271 --> 00:10:00.621
RUTHERFORD :
What? Oh, man,

00:10:00.664 --> 00:10:02.666
I would kill to work
on the deflector dish.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.103
Most of my day is spent
repairing food replicators.

00:10:05.147 --> 00:10:07.366
-They really break that often?
-Only when you get food in 'em.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.498
Ah, at least
you don't have to be around

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:09.499
Lieutenant Commander Billups.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:10.761
Knowing how to talk to women

00:10:10.805 --> 00:10:13.111
is kind of that guy's
final frontier.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.462
-That is illogical!
-Oh! S-Sorry.

00:10:16.506 --> 00:10:17.681
I-Is he a friend of yours?

00:10:17.725 --> 00:10:19.640
No, no, no, no--
it's this Vulcan implant.

00:10:19.683 --> 00:10:21.642
It keeps on randomly suppressing
my emotional reactions.

00:10:21.685 --> 00:10:23.469
Sorry if this
is making it weird.

00:10:23.513 --> 00:10:25.428
I'm just not used
to being a cyborg yet.

00:10:25.471 --> 00:10:27.648
Actually, my dad was a cyborg.

00:10:29.737 --> 00:10:31.434
Shaxs drop his latte again?

00:10:31.477 --> 00:10:33.523
Guy's got baby hands.
-No.

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.525
"Computer, send me a suck-up
to clean up my mess.

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:37.527
I have a giant torso
and little hands. Over."

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.443
- Right?
-Yeah, hilarious.

00:10:42.358 --> 00:10:45.274
BILLUPS:
All right, people,
you know the plan.

00:10:45.317 --> 00:10:49.757
Let's get this array set up
so the, uh, "Galardonians"

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.194
can communicate with the rest
of the Federation.

00:10:55.806 --> 00:10:58.156
Oh, man, this is really nice.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.332
I'm glad we got to sit down
and get to know each other

00:11:00.376 --> 00:11:01.507
without any interruptions.

00:11:19.134 --> 00:11:21.353
CREWMAN:
Set phasers to stun!

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:25.662
So, where are you quartered?

00:11:25.706 --> 00:11:28.709
Deck Nine, by the squash courts.

00:11:28.752 --> 00:11:30.798
Someone brought a virus
back from the planet.

00:11:30.841 --> 00:11:34.671
This is happening
all over the ship.

00:11:34.715 --> 00:11:36.760
I've never played squash.
Is it fun?

00:11:36.804 --> 00:11:38.719
We should play sometime.

00:11:43.854 --> 00:11:45.551
Oh, yeah, it's all gonna be
over subspace.

00:11:45.595 --> 00:11:47.597
You're gonna love it.

00:11:55.474 --> 00:11:56.519
Unbelievable.

00:12:02.351 --> 00:12:04.309
Hey, you. Green girl!

00:12:04.353 --> 00:12:05.920
Strap patients down
as they come in.

00:12:05.963 --> 00:12:07.704
Double them up if you have to.
They aren't going to infect

00:12:07.748 --> 00:12:10.402
-each other twice.
-But, uh, uh,

00:12:10.446 --> 00:12:12.709
I was actually supposed to be
assisting Nurse Westlake.

00:12:12.753 --> 00:12:14.798
That isNurse Westlake.

00:12:16.844 --> 00:12:19.803
Wow, it's such an honor
to meet you, sir.

00:12:19.847 --> 00:12:22.588
I'm looking forward
to working with you.

00:12:27.898 --> 00:12:29.465
-Aha!

00:12:29.508 --> 00:12:30.858
Boimler!
Ugh, don't jump out at people.

00:12:30.901 --> 00:12:33.338
For real, man. You're lucky
I didn't phaser you.

00:12:33.382 --> 00:12:35.471
You're selling Federation
weapons to these guys,

00:12:35.514 --> 00:12:36.733
-aren't you?
-Yo, calm down.

00:12:36.777 --> 00:12:38.256
No!

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.606
I'm sick of you
pushing me around!

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.435
Explain yourself right here!

00:12:43.479 --> 00:12:44.915
Boims, you need to shut up.
Listen to me.

00:12:44.959 --> 00:12:46.438
You know nothing.
Shut your mouth.

00:12:46.482 --> 00:12:48.179
Uh, we're just gonna take off.

00:12:48.223 --> 00:12:50.442
-Nobody move!

00:12:50.486 --> 00:12:52.836
Selling Starfleet technology
without the express consent

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:55.491
of the Federation Council
is a breach of regulations

00:12:55.534 --> 00:12:56.927
498 and 756 of...

00:12:56.971 --> 00:12:59.582
And regulations 25, 15, 348.

00:12:59.625 --> 00:13:01.889
You're breaking 76 just
for pointing that phaser at me.

00:13:01.932 --> 00:13:03.629
Fine, you know
more regulations than me.

00:13:03.673 --> 00:13:04.805
I still have to stop you.

00:13:04.848 --> 00:13:06.676
It's farm equipment, you idiot.

00:13:06.719 --> 00:13:08.634
-They're farmers.
-I'm not an idiot.

00:13:08.678 --> 00:13:10.723
You expect me
to believe that...?

00:13:10.767 --> 00:13:12.682
Shovel and hoe?

00:13:20.864 --> 00:13:22.518
Run, idiot!

00:13:30.395 --> 00:13:31.701
What's it doing?

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:33.659
It's shooting butt-webbing
at a tree.

00:13:33.703 --> 00:13:34.965
I-It looks pretty pissed.

00:13:35.009 --> 00:13:35.966
Well, I hope you're happy.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:37.838
You left your post.

00:13:37.881 --> 00:13:40.579
Oh, I am so sorry I made sure
that some humble farmers,

00:13:40.623 --> 00:13:42.712
who can't afford to wait
for Starfleet bureaucracy

00:13:42.755 --> 00:13:44.845
to notice them, got some help
so they didn't have to starve.

00:13:44.888 --> 00:13:46.672
How did you even know
these guys exist?

00:13:51.677 --> 00:13:54.767
Because I was here for first
contact last year on the Quito,

00:13:54.811 --> 00:13:57.640
before I got my ass demoted
and transferred to the Cerritos.

00:13:57.683 --> 00:13:59.772
Well, I didn't know that.

00:13:59.816 --> 00:14:02.775
I have served on five ships,
man. I have seen stuff.

00:14:02.819 --> 00:14:04.690
One time, I got trapped
in a sentient cave for weeks.

00:14:04.734 --> 00:14:06.823
You ever been trapped
in a sentient cave?

00:14:06.867 --> 00:14:08.912
That's a dark place
that knows things.

00:14:08.956 --> 00:14:11.567
I almost got my head taken off
by a singing crystal.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.743
I've been in a Klingon prison
where I had to fight a yeti

00:14:13.786 --> 00:14:15.701
for my own shoes for no reason.

00:14:15.745 --> 00:14:17.355
He was just being a dick.

00:14:17.399 --> 00:14:18.530
You've been on, what,
four planets?

00:14:18.574 --> 00:14:20.706
Five, if you include Vulcan.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:21.794
Of course I don't
include stupid Vulcan.

00:14:21.838 --> 00:14:22.926
You may as well count Earth.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:24.841
I wascounting Earth.

00:14:24.885 --> 00:14:27.931
You don't know anything
except what's in your manuals.

00:14:27.975 --> 00:14:29.715
Since you can't think
for yourself, how about you

00:14:29.759 --> 00:14:31.413
follow my lead, and maybe
we'll get out of this alive?

00:14:31.456 --> 00:14:33.937
Ensign Boimler to Cerritos.
Two for emergency trans...

00:14:36.374 --> 00:14:37.941
Are you insane?

00:14:37.985 --> 00:14:40.030
We can't just beam out of here.
These guys need that animal.

00:14:40.074 --> 00:14:42.815
-Even if it eats us?
-General Order 5.

00:14:42.859 --> 00:14:44.513
Fine, okay.
How about we stun it?

00:14:44.556 --> 00:14:46.689
-We'll just stun it.
-No. That could spoil the milk.

00:14:46.732 --> 00:14:48.386
-Spoil what milk?
-These guys probably milk it.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.779
-Oh, like you even know.
- Ooh.

00:14:49.822 --> 00:14:51.868
-Take off your pants.
- Mariner.

00:14:53.043 --> 00:14:54.958
-Five ships.

00:14:55.002 --> 00:14:56.699
Yeti shoes. I am always right.

00:14:56.742 --> 00:14:58.440
Take them off now.

00:15:04.359 --> 00:15:05.969
MARINER:
Yes, it's working.

00:15:06.013 --> 00:15:08.580
Man, look at that thing
just tear into that dummy.

00:15:08.624 --> 00:15:10.060
Okay, here we go,
get ready to jump.

00:15:10.104 --> 00:15:11.366
Wait, why isn't it
attacking youruniform?

00:15:11.409 --> 00:15:13.585
It's going to town on mine.

00:15:13.629 --> 00:15:15.674
-Random chance? Who cares?
On my mark.
-I care.

00:15:15.718 --> 00:15:17.850
I say we wait for it
to destroy both of our uniforms.

00:15:17.894 --> 00:15:19.026
Mark!

00:15:20.027 --> 00:15:21.593
Jump, Boimler!

00:15:21.637 --> 00:15:22.986
Come on, it's safe.
It can't reach back this far.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.596
Man.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:25.946
Oh!

00:15:25.989 --> 00:15:27.948
Phaser it! Phaser it! Phaser it!

00:15:27.991 --> 00:15:30.385
Please don't phaser her.
It'll spoil the milk.

00:15:30.428 --> 00:15:31.952
Did you hear that?

00:15:31.995 --> 00:15:34.084
-Uh, I can't let it eat him.
-She's an herbivore.

00:15:34.128 --> 00:15:36.608
She's just gumming on him
to suckle out some moisture.

00:15:36.652 --> 00:15:39.002
Oh, okay.
Hey, Brad. Good news, buddy.

00:15:39.046 --> 00:15:41.918
So, I've ju-- it's just suckling
you, I've just learned.

00:15:41.962 --> 00:15:43.615
-You're fine.
-Help!

00:15:43.659 --> 00:15:45.400
Hang in there, you got this.
It is getting tired.

00:15:45.443 --> 00:15:47.532
So go to your happy place,
like, ooh,

00:15:47.576 --> 00:15:49.056
think about the warp core.

00:15:50.666 --> 00:15:52.059
You, uh, want a snack
or something?

00:15:52.102 --> 00:15:54.322
Yeah, you got any of that milk?

00:15:54.365 --> 00:15:56.367
SHAXS:
All uninfected crew meet
at Transporter Room Eight.

00:15:56.411 --> 00:15:58.543
We have to get
to the rally point.

00:15:58.587 --> 00:16:01.068
I guess we better go for a walk.

00:16:04.158 --> 00:16:06.377
RUTHERFORD:
There's a maintenance hatch
on the other side of the saucer

00:16:06.421 --> 00:16:08.771
that should give us access
to Deck Eight.

00:16:08.814 --> 00:16:10.120
What kind of music are you into?

00:16:10.164 --> 00:16:11.730
We have just enough oxygen
to get there,

00:16:11.774 --> 00:16:13.384
but we're cutting it close.

00:16:13.428 --> 00:16:15.996
I really like this classical
band called The Monkees.

00:16:16.039 --> 00:16:17.345
Ever heard of 'em?

00:16:17.388 --> 00:16:18.694
Let's just say "I'm a Believer."

00:16:49.725 --> 00:16:52.554
Mmm. Wow. I wasn't
expecting that.

00:16:52.597 --> 00:16:53.903
What did you expect?

00:16:53.946 --> 00:16:55.122
Well, for these maintenance
hatch doors

00:16:55.165 --> 00:16:56.558
to recognize our combadges.

00:16:56.601 --> 00:16:59.691
Oh, no, I mean
what just happened?

00:16:59.735 --> 00:17:02.085
I'm more worried about
what didn't just happen.

00:17:02.129 --> 00:17:04.044
Failure analysis estimates
the reliability

00:17:04.087 --> 00:17:07.090
of this mechanism
at one out of 4.69 repeating.

00:17:07.134 --> 00:17:09.527
-Oh, are you seeing this?

00:17:11.442 --> 00:17:13.096
-The anesthetic is useless.

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:15.098
We have to work through
the pain. Your hands clean?

00:17:15.142 --> 00:17:17.579
-Uh...
-Pump this. Don't pass out.

00:17:17.622 --> 00:17:19.842
Nobody's authorized to pass out!

00:17:19.885 --> 00:17:22.105
That's my heart!
It hurts when you pump it!

00:17:22.149 --> 00:17:23.541
-Oh, God! Oh...
-Sorry.

00:17:23.585 --> 00:17:26.631
-Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
-Oh, God. Oh!

00:17:33.943 --> 00:17:37.207
Okay, there we go, man, yeah.

00:17:37.251 --> 00:17:39.209
See? I told you it'd be okay.

00:17:39.253 --> 00:17:41.429
My bones.

00:17:41.472 --> 00:17:42.734
You'll be fine.
Doc'll wave a light over it.

00:17:42.778 --> 00:17:43.953
We got to get back to camp.

00:17:43.996 --> 00:17:45.085
You took way too long
with that thing.

00:17:45.128 --> 00:17:48.740
-But I'm naked.

00:17:51.178 --> 00:17:53.702
At least we got
to help those guys.

00:17:53.745 --> 00:17:55.443
I think we make
a pretty good team, Boimler.

00:17:55.486 --> 00:17:57.967
You may as well know,
I've been monitoring you.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.186
I'm supposed to report
any breach of conduct

00:17:59.229 --> 00:18:00.752
to the captain.

00:18:00.796 --> 00:18:02.493
We've been serving together
for a year,

00:18:02.537 --> 00:18:04.191
and I still don't get
why you worship those guys.

00:18:04.234 --> 00:18:05.235
They're heroes.

00:18:05.279 --> 00:18:06.802
All they care about is glory.

00:18:06.845 --> 00:18:08.934
Stuff that could earn them
a mention in the history books.

00:18:08.978 --> 00:18:10.197
They don't really care about us.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.981
No way, no.
The captain tries her hardest

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:14.114
to support all of us, she just
doesn't always have time to...

00:18:14.157 --> 00:18:15.463
Look, I don't have
to defend her.

00:18:15.506 --> 00:18:16.986
You're not gonna talk me out
of reporting you.

00:18:24.776 --> 00:18:26.952
-Whoa! What the hell?

00:18:26.996 --> 00:18:29.825
Keep the doors secure.
The crew depends on us.

00:18:29.868 --> 00:18:32.132
-We can't let them down.

00:18:33.655 --> 00:18:35.047
Captain, I'm sure
you're wondering

00:18:35.091 --> 00:18:36.658
-where my uniform is.
-Shaxs, what are my options?

00:18:36.701 --> 00:18:38.921
I recommend we detonate
the entire warp core, Captain.

00:18:38.964 --> 00:18:40.227
-What? No.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.880
We need to get this man
to sickbay immediately.

00:18:41.924 --> 00:18:43.621
He is very important.

00:18:43.665 --> 00:18:44.796
What makes him so special?

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:45.884
Nothing. He's worthless.

00:18:45.928 --> 00:18:47.625
It's the slime, Captain.

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:50.585
He's covered in slime
that could save us all.

00:18:50.628 --> 00:18:53.283
Everyone, protect this slime.

00:19:14.217 --> 00:19:16.001
T'ANA:
Holy .

00:19:16.045 --> 00:19:19.222
This substance completely
neutralizes the rage effect.

00:19:19.266 --> 00:19:20.615
It came
from this spider cow thing.

00:19:20.658 --> 00:19:21.833
I-I could tell you all about it.

00:19:21.877 --> 00:19:24.184
But can you synthesize
a cure, Doctor?

00:19:24.227 --> 00:19:26.664
Hmm. I better.
You don't have much time.

00:19:26.708 --> 00:19:28.231
Ooh, should've washed
those hands, Captain.

00:19:28.275 --> 00:19:29.754
Stow it, Mariner.

00:19:31.234 --> 00:19:33.193
Ah, ah, ah...

00:19:33.236 --> 00:19:35.543
Oh, what happened? Where am I?

00:19:35.586 --> 00:19:37.849
And did I eat flesh?

00:19:37.893 --> 00:19:40.200
-Uh, hardly any.
-How much did I eat?!

00:19:49.252 --> 00:19:51.689
-It's working!
-Looks like you'll get
to publish

00:19:51.733 --> 00:19:53.256
more award-winning
research, Doc.

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:56.172
-Great, more paperwork.

00:19:56.216 --> 00:19:57.869
RANSOM:
How much did I eat?

00:19:57.913 --> 00:19:59.567
Uh, this guy saved your asses.
Ensign Brad Boimler.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.133
Put thatin the paperwork.

00:20:02.961 --> 00:20:05.137
Still, uh, happy to be here?

00:20:05.181 --> 00:20:08.880
Are you kidding?
I got to hold a heart!

00:20:11.231 --> 00:20:13.885
FREEMAN:
Once again, solely thanks
to the brilliant efforts

00:20:13.929 --> 00:20:15.278
of Dr. T'Ana,

00:20:15.322 --> 00:20:16.888
the crew is saved.

00:20:16.932 --> 00:20:19.282
Undetected
by the first contact team,

00:20:19.326 --> 00:20:22.720
the alien virus is exactly
the type of eventuality

00:20:22.764 --> 00:20:25.288
that can make
a second contact mission

00:20:25.332 --> 00:20:27.377
a life-or-death situation.

00:20:27.421 --> 00:20:30.380
Luckily, my senior staff
are always up for a challenge.

00:20:30.424 --> 00:20:32.643
End recording.

00:20:32.687 --> 00:20:33.644
Sorry about that,
Ensign Bumford.

00:20:33.688 --> 00:20:34.645
What do you have to report?

00:20:34.689 --> 00:20:36.734
-Boimler.
-Pardon?

00:20:36.778 --> 00:20:38.214
It's Boimler, not Bumford.

00:20:38.258 --> 00:20:40.738
Wha-What about Mariner?
Did she follow protocol?

00:20:40.782 --> 00:20:42.697
Yeah, I think so.
We spent the whole day

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:44.655
just adjusting
the subspace comm array.

00:20:44.699 --> 00:20:46.614
This says you came back
covered in bite marks,

00:20:46.657 --> 00:20:47.919
wearing an alien frock.

00:20:47.963 --> 00:20:49.791
What, she had nothing
to do with that?

00:20:49.834 --> 00:20:52.010
You know, I don't remember much.

00:20:52.054 --> 00:20:54.317
Maybe that goo
that saved the ship

00:20:54.361 --> 00:20:55.840
messed with my memory.

00:20:55.884 --> 00:20:57.407
Nothing insubordinate?

00:20:57.451 --> 00:20:59.148
-Not that I saw.
-Unbelievable.

00:20:59.191 --> 00:21:02.064
Thank you, Ensign Boimler.

00:21:02.107 --> 00:21:04.284
Dismissed.

00:21:05.981 --> 00:21:08.113
Everything all right,
Captain Freeman?

00:21:08.157 --> 00:21:10.420
I heard you had some sort
of rage virus?

00:21:10.464 --> 00:21:12.292
Ransom tried to eat a guy.
We're fine.

00:21:12.335 --> 00:21:13.815
Listen, I've had enough.

00:21:13.858 --> 00:21:15.469
I'm throwing her in the brig.

00:21:15.512 --> 00:21:17.035
We already tried that.
You know it doesn't work.

00:21:17.079 --> 00:21:19.037
-She loves the brig.
-She undermines me

00:21:19.081 --> 00:21:21.997
-in front of the crew!
-I'm sure nobody notices.

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:24.434
-Yeah, they do.
-Sweetheart, just...

00:21:24.478 --> 00:21:26.131
Don't you "sweetheart" me.
We agreed, if she

00:21:26.175 --> 00:21:28.046
didn't fit in here, you'd
send her back to the Quito.

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.744
Well, she doesn't fit in!

00:21:29.787 --> 00:21:31.833
I got to go.
Admiral stuff. Love you.

00:21:31.876 --> 00:21:33.835
Don't you hang up on me!
She's your daughter, too!

00:21:33.878 --> 00:21:35.358
-Hanging up now.
-Don't you dare.

00:21:35.402 --> 00:21:36.620
-Finger's on the button.
-Don't you... don't you...

00:21:36.664 --> 00:21:37.752
-Uh, I-I'm losing you.
-I said don't...

00:21:37.795 --> 00:21:40.320
Oh, no. Did the rage virus
ruin your date?

00:21:40.363 --> 00:21:42.322
Nah, that stuff happens
all the time.

00:21:42.365 --> 00:21:44.802
Oh, good. So, was she
as great as everyone says?

00:21:44.846 --> 00:21:46.369
Yeah. She was smart and pretty

00:21:46.413 --> 00:21:49.329
and, ooh, highly effective
in a ship-wide crisis.

00:21:49.372 --> 00:21:51.113
So, tell me,
are you guys a thing?

00:21:51.156 --> 00:21:53.333
-Yeah, I'm not seeing her again.
-Well, you survived

00:21:53.376 --> 00:21:54.856
an epic life-threatening
situation together.

00:21:54.899 --> 00:21:56.858
-Don't you share a bond?
-Oh, for sure.

00:21:56.901 --> 00:21:59.208
But she had zero interest
in figuring out why a red alert

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:01.428
overrode Maintenance Hatch 70's
access protocols.

00:22:01.471 --> 00:22:03.430
It's, like,
can you even imagine?

00:22:03.473 --> 00:22:05.345
I-I'm sorry. What?

00:22:05.388 --> 00:22:07.999
-It did?!
-Yes. I mean,
who has time for romance

00:22:08.043 --> 00:22:09.697
when there's
a level two diagnostic

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:11.351
just sitting there
waiting to be run?

00:22:11.394 --> 00:22:13.004
Mm-mm.
Don't have to tell me twice.

00:22:13.048 --> 00:22:14.484
I am right there.

00:22:14.528 --> 00:22:16.704
-Mariner.
- Boimler.

00:22:16.747 --> 00:22:18.749
I wanted to thank you.

00:22:18.793 --> 00:22:20.229
It felt good
helping those people.

00:22:20.272 --> 00:22:21.752
I mean, you might be...

00:22:21.796 --> 00:22:23.406
Mm, better than you
in every single way?

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:25.887
Unorthodox, but--
I can't believe I'm saying it--

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:28.150
Starfleet is better
with you in it.

00:22:28.193 --> 00:22:30.108
Wait, so you
didn't tattle on me?

00:22:30.152 --> 00:22:31.196
I did not.

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:33.416
Boimler! Wha...?
No way, man!

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:35.200
I had you pegged wrong.

00:22:35.244 --> 00:22:37.420
Yeah, I thought you were,
like, a boring worker drone.

00:22:37.464 --> 00:22:39.422
And you are,
but inside that drone is

00:22:39.466 --> 00:22:41.990
an ambitious little weasel,
and inside that weasel

00:22:42.033 --> 00:22:44.209
might be a tiny human being.

00:22:44.253 --> 00:22:45.776
That's, uh, sort of unfair.

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:47.474
This is a moment, man.
Ooh, this is a mood.

00:22:47.517 --> 00:22:49.432
Okay? And I do not care
how long it takes,

00:22:49.476 --> 00:22:51.391
we're going to get your butt
in a captain's chair.

00:22:51.434 --> 00:22:53.001
-This isn't a big deal.
-Mm, guess what.

00:22:53.044 --> 00:22:54.089
I'm your new mentor. Boom.

00:22:54.132 --> 00:22:55.525
Surprise, bitch, it's done.

00:22:55.569 --> 00:22:57.832
-How does it feel?
-No, you can't just decide.

00:22:57.875 --> 00:22:59.529
-Whoa. She's your mentor?
-No, she's not.
-Come on, guys! Lower decks!

00:22:59.573 --> 00:23:01.226
-Lower decks! Lower decks!
-Congrats, man.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.011
-TENDI: That's cool.
-MARINER: Teamwork! Spirit!

00:23:03.054 --> 00:23:05.056
Community!
Lower decks! Lower decks!

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:07.058
Lower decks!
You're gonna be my cha'DIch

00:23:07.102 --> 00:23:08.886
-from now on, baby!
-I don't want lessons from you.

00:23:08.930 --> 00:23:10.235
Okay, Klingons?
They're all about fighting.

00:23:10.279 --> 00:23:11.193
They're always making oaths
about everything.

00:23:11.236 --> 00:23:12.194
Everyone knows that.

00:23:12.237 --> 00:23:13.369
Do you know about Spock?

00:23:13.413 --> 00:23:14.762
Dude came back...
from being dead!

00:23:14.805 --> 00:23:16.111
Yeah, I think
I've heard of Spock.

00:23:16.154 --> 00:23:17.460
He got frickin' Genesis-deviced
and fought Khan

00:23:17.504 --> 00:23:18.896
-and some space whales!
-Can we just go back

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:20.245
-to not being friends?
-How about Sulu?

00:23:20.289 --> 00:23:22.073
Ooh, he rocked a sword.
That was his thing.

00:23:22.117 --> 00:23:24.075
That could be your thing, too!
We're due for a new sword guy!

00:23:24.119 --> 00:23:25.903
BOIMLER:
What can I do
to make this stop, please?

00:23:25.947 --> 00:23:27.905
-MARINER: Mm, do you know Kirk? My man Worf?
-Yes. Yes!

00:23:27.949 --> 00:23:29.820
-MARINER: Gary Mitchell?
-I'm sure I could look him up.

00:23:29.864 --> 00:23:31.648
MARINER: You don't have to,
because you have a mentor!

00:23:31.692 --> 00:23:33.389
-BOIMLER: No. Don't touch me.
-Do you know Deanna Troi?

00:23:33.433 --> 00:23:35.478
Her body be bangin'!
She went from a jumpsuit...

00:25:12.662 --> 00:25:15.883
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:26:04.148 --> 00:26:05.149
Chirp.
